/* ================================================================ ATWS: anticipated transient without scram ================================================================
   The trip breakers are stuck shut. When a trip signal comes in the rods stay out: the turbine trips (AMSAC), the plant heats up and
   pressure climbs, and only the negative moderator temperature coefficient holds power back. FR-S.1: try a manual trip, make sure the
   turbine is tripped and aux feed is running, open the rod drive MG set breakers so the grippers let go, and emergency borate. */
Object.assign(TRIPS, { MG: 'Rod drive MG sets de-energised (ATWS recovery)', SEIS: 'Seismic trip (ground acceleration high)' });
Object.assign(TRIPWHY, { MG: 'The automatic trip failed (an ATWS). The rods went in when the rod drive motor-generator sets were switched off, so the grippers lost power and let go.', SEIS: 'The seismic monitors saw strong ground acceleration and tripped the reactor automatically, before the shaking could damage anything.' });
FAULT.list.push({ id: 'atws', t: 'ATWS: trip breakers stuck', d: 'The reactor trip breakers are mechanically stuck shut. About 25 s after this goes in, both main feed pumps trip.', see: 'The feed loss brings a trip signal (first-out lights), but the rods stay out and power stays up. AMSAC trips the turbine, so the reactor coolant heats up: pressuriser pressure climbs and the PORVs lift. The negative moderator temperature coefficient pulls power down a bit, but not to zero.', resp: 'FR-S.1. Try a manual trip (it will fail). Check the turbine has tripped and aux feed is running. On the ATWS card, <b>open the rod drive MG set breakers</b>: the grippers lose power and the rods fall. If you can’t, drive the rods in on MANUAL and start <b>EMERGENCY BORATE</b> (board 3).' });
CRISIS.pool.push('atws');
